(footprint "MiniDIN6_PS2_Socket_CUI_MD-60S"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "amigahid-pico-rev6")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Mini-DIN 6-pin (PS/2) female PCB socket, right-angle THT, Same Sky / CUI Devices MD-60S; hole grid also matches Kycon KMDGX-6S. Amiga A4000 keyboard connector, which uses the PS/2 pin positions exactly: 1=KDAT 3=GND 4=+5V 5=KCLK, 2 and 6 NC. Dimensions from the Same Sky MD-S series datasheet dated 09/12/2024, page 3, MD-60S Recommended PCB Layout / Top View / Date Codes after 03/03/2022, https://www.sameskydevices.com/product/resource/md-s.pdf : 6 x 0.9 +0.1/-0 mm dia holes, row 4/2/1/3 at 8.50 mm and row 6/5 at 11.00 mm from the mating face, outer columns 6.80 mm apart and the inner pair 2.60 mm apart, earth-terminal slot 2.2 x 0.7 mm on the centreline 4.70 mm from the face, body 14.0 x 12.4 x 12.8 mm. Cross-checked against Kycon KMDGX-xS-N rev B5 (03/28/18) 6-position Recommended PCB Layout (Bottom View), https://www.kycon.com/Pub_Eng_Draw/KMDGX-xS-N.pdf , which gives the same grid with 1.10 mm dia holes and a 2.30 mm dia locating boss in place of the earth tab (Kycon grid numbers map to standard pins as 1=1 2=2 3=3 5=4 6=5 8=6). Holes are drilled 1.10 mm and the centre feature is one plated 2.40 mm hole (pad SH) that clears both the CUI earth tab and the Kycon boss. Anchor (0,0) = centre of the mating face plane - place it on the board edge line. VERIFY AGAINST A PHYSICAL SAMPLE BEFORE FAB.")
	(tags "connector mini-din minidin md-60s kmdgx ps2 ps/2 6-pin socket receptacle right-angle tht amiga keyboard a4000 amigahid rev6")
